Q: How to code a car shape of a F1 car moving on a track like F1 circuit A: <p>The car stays on the path using this pattern:</p>
<pre><code>const angle = Math.atan2(target.y - car.y, target.x - car.x);
car.x += Math.cos(angle) * speed;
car.y += Math.sin(angle) * speed;

if (distanceTo(target) &lt; threshold) {
  index = (index + 1) % waypoints.length;
  if (index === 0) lapCount++;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Define waypoints around your circuit shape, and the car automatically follows them. More waypoints = smoother path.</p>
<p>Here's a demo you can see : <a href="https://github.com/codewithanshuman/F1-Circuit-Simulator" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/codewithanshuman/F1-Circuit-Simulator</a></p>

Q: How to join two tables using JPA Criteria Builder? A: <p>This is how I do it</p>

<pre><code>    EntityManager em = emf.createEntityManager();
    CriteriaBuilder cb = em.getCriteriaBuilder();
    CriteriaQuery&lt;Object&gt; cq = cb.createQuery();
    Root&lt;Item&gt; ri = cq.from(School.class);

    // joins
    Join&lt;Object, Object&gt; h = ri.join("Student");
    Query query = em.createQuery(cq);
    List&lt;Object[]&gt; result = query.getResultList();
</code></pre>

